---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ControlledEvaluationFlow from "../components/diagrams/ControlledEvaluationFlow.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Controlled Evaluation | BeaconGuard Architecture Review"
  description="Request a bounded BeaconGuard Controlled Evaluation covering boundary placement, identity and trust mapping, Compliance Playbook controls, ALLOW and DENY cases, evidence review, and deployment-fit qualification."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <h1>Controlled Evaluation</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A Controlled Evaluation is a bounded architecture review for one regulated workflow. It validates Runtime Control Boundary placement, Compliance Playbook mapping, ALLOW and DENY cases, Verifiable Decision Records, and deployment fit without replacing existing systems of record.
    </p>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard is currently in controlled internal qualification across enterprise security, identity, evidence integrity, deployment operations, recovery, and cross-platform packaging. Customer-specific architecture and deployment-fit reviews are available through this bounded evaluation model.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Not a rip-and-replace proposal</h2>
    <p>
      Existing applications continue to own workflow logic and records. BeaconGuard is evaluated as a deterministic control and evidence boundary before governed execution.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Inputs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One bounded regulated workflow</li>
      <li>Representative request contract</li>
      <li>Workforce and workload identity assumptions</li>
      <li>Tenant and environment boundaries</li>
      <li>Required trust context</li>
      <li>Compliance Playbook controls</li>
      <li>Evidence and retention expectations</li>
      <li>Target deployment assumptions</li>
      <li>Recovery and rollback expectations</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Controlled Evaluation workflow</h2>
    <ControlledEvaluationFlow />
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Activities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Runtime boundary placement</li>
      <li>System Connector fit</li>
      <li>Request-authenticity mapping</li>
      <li>Identity and service-identity mapping</li>
      <li>Tenant and environment isolation review</li>
      <li>Compliance Playbook mapping</li>
      <li>ALLOW and DENY case design</li>
      <li>Post-DENY governance review scenario design (review does not permit execution)</li>
      <li>Replay and duplicate-request analysis</li>
      <li>Evidence-provider and retention review</li>
      <li>Installation-target preflight</li>
      <li>Release and package identity verification</li>
      <li>Backup, restore, rollback, and recovery planning</li>
      <li>Responsibility and operational-acceptance review</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section" aria-labelledby="controlled-demo-card-title">
    <div class="content-card proof-demo-card">
      <p class="section-label">CONTROLLED DEMONSTRATION</p>
      <h2 id="controlled-demo-card-title">See the BeaconGuard Review Process in Operation</h2>
      <p>
        Watch a controlled example of deterministic denial, reviewer step-up authentication, bounded one-time authorization, a new governed request, and rejection of authorization reuse.
      </p>
      <p>
        The demonstration provides a preview of the enforcement and evidence behavior that enterprise reviewers can examine during a bounded Controlled Evaluation.
      </p>
      <div class="page-actions">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/proof-evidence#beaconguard-review-process">Watch the Review Process</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Outputs</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Architecture-fit memo</li>
      <li>Control responsibility matrix</li>
      <li>Identity and trust-boundary map</li>
      <li>Compliance Playbook or mapping artifact</li>
      <li>Sample Verifiable Decision Records</li>
      <li>Deployment qualification assessment</li>
      <li>Recovery and rollback considerations</li>
      <li>Blocker register</li>
      <li>Next-step recommendation</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Who should participate</h2>
    <div class="section-grid section-grid--compact">
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Healthcare</h3>
        <p>Teams owning PHI-sensitive operational AI pathways and privacy review obligations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Financial services</h3>
        <p>Teams owning AML, KYC, fraud, dispute, or customer-impacting recommendation workflows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-card">
        <h3>Regulated internal automation</h3>
        <p>Teams placing agents or automations against production systems under fail-closed controls.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Contact the team</h2>
    <p>
      Timing and commercial terms are confirmed during intake. Do not submit PHI, customer records, credentials, production secrets, or confidential evidence in the initial message.
    </p>
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact">Request Controlled Evaluation</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/platform">Review platform overview</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
